15 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Principal Coordinates Analysis \(PCoA\) plots depicting Bray-Curtis distances. The top plot shows variation based on sampling time points \(days 3, 9, 17, 23, 31, and 37\) with different colored points for each day. The bottom plot shows variation based on added alkalinity levels \(0 to 1250 micromoles per liter\), with shades of blue indicating increasing alkalinity. Both plots display Axis 1 \(29%\) against Axis 2 \(14.4%\) and include a color legend for day and alkalinity level.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Principal Coordinates Analysis \(PCoA\) plots show the distribution of community structures across three panels: entire, core, and transient communities. Each panel includes colored dots representing sampling times, with Axis.1 and Axis.2 showing variance percentages. The sampling times, indicated by colors, are gray \(3\), green \(9\), orange \(17\), blue \(23\), pink \(31\), and light green \(37\).) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Scatter plot and bar chart showing K-means clustering analysis of microbial communities. The scatter plot on the left categorizes data points into three clusters: red for Cluster 1, green for Cluster 2, and blue for Cluster 3. The bar chart on the right displays microbial community proportions by family level, with categories including Alteromonadaceae, Clade I, Flavobacteriaceae, Rhodobacteraceae, and others. Each bar represents a cluster, illustrating family distribution within each cluster.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Stacked bar chart showing proportions of KEGG metabolic pathways at baseline and treatment levels. Pathways include ABC transporters, amino acids biosynthesis, antibiotics biosynthesis, secondary metabolites biosynthesis, carbon metabolism, metabolic pathways, microbial metabolism, quorum sensing, two-component system, and others. ) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Grid of six bar charts showing cross-correlation with added alkalinity at different deltas, ranging from zero to one thousand two hundred fifty. Red and blue bars represent varying strengths of correlation at different lags.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (12 panels grid of line graphs. Each panel is specifying a mesocosm. The X achsis shows the day of the experiment increasing from left to right.  There are two y achsis and two lines. The brown line shows trends in bacterial cell counts and the blue line shows trends in chlorophyll a concentrations.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
